# Canon data vs lore docs

## Non-negotiables

- Numeric rank policy lives **only** in `addon/ChurchOfBeef/Data/Ranks.lua` → `COB.Ranks`
- `docs/canon/` is flavor prose — if a number appears, delete it and point at `Data/Ranks.lua`
- Do not invent a top-level `canon/` Lua package (TOC loads only inside the addon folder)

## Machine canon owns

Rank `id` / `title` / `threshold` / `kind`, `CouncilSeats`, `ProphetUnique`, `OfficerRankIndexMax`, helpers (`Threshold`, `IsPointDriven`, `Title`).

```lua
-- ✅
local title = COB.Ranks.Title(rankId)
local need = COB.Ranks.Threshold(2)

-- ❌ hardcoding policy in UI/Core
local need = 50
```

Kinds: `points` (1–5), `council`, `prophet`. Seat/uniqueness via `kind` (see `Core/Ladder.lua`).

## SavedVariables are not canon

`ChurchOfBeefDB` (`Core/DB.lua`) caches local standing, promote suggestions, and UI prefs. Church titles come from the live guild roster (`Core/Roster` + `Ranks.ChurchRankIdForGuildIndex`), not from SV.
